<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/108833%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Gallo-Roman Sanctuary at Bû";
    rdfs:comment "Remains of a rectangular Romano-Celtic temple were excavated north of the French town of Bû (in the department of Eure-et-Loir), beginning in the 1960s. Other buildings of uncertain nature and a theater were also identified in the vicinity. Coins and pottery discovered at the site indicate there was activity there during the Roman imperial period.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/108833> .

