<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/109342090%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Temple of Peltuinum";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413247%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Temple of Peltuinum is located on the forum square; its final iteration was that of a Corinthian hexastyle prostyle sanctuary of the Roman phase of the city, when the shrine may have been dedicated to Apollo. The sanctuary also may have had a pre-Roman phase connected with a sacred spring.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/109342090> .

