<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/113543066%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Solucar Albayda";
    rdfs:comment "A Spanish village located to the west of Sevilla, Spain. In the thirteenth century, it belonged to the kingdom of Alfonso X. The modern toponym is a derivation of the Arabic toponym \"Solucar Al-bayda\", meaning \"the white one\". The site was known as Sanlúcar de Albaida until it took the definitive name of Albaida de Aljarafe.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/113543066> .

