<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/114773%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Clanum";
    rdfs:comment "A road station listed in the Antonine Itineraries on the Agedincum → Augustobona road. It is perhaps to be localized in the modern French commune of Paisy-Cosdon (Aube department), where ceramic fragments of Gallo-Roman date and associated stone architectural elements were identified in a construction excavation in the 20th century.";
