<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/116348460%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Eʾesirkalama";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/633091639%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893951%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The temple of the god Pisangunuk, Eʾesirkalama (“House of the Street of the Land”), was located in the Kumar district of Babylon, in the western half of the inner city. According to the Babylonian topographical text Tintir = Babylon Tablet IV, it was one of seven temples in that part of Babylon.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/116348460> .

