<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/117946902%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Enamtila";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/633091639%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893951%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The temple of the god Bēl-mātāti (Enlil), Enamtila (“House of Life”), was located in the Kumar district of Babylon, in the western half of the inner city. According to the Babylonian topographical text Tintir = Babylon Tablet IV, it was one of seven temples in that part of Babylon. Enamtila is mentioned in Old Babylonian and Kassite Period texts.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/117946902> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/117946902/bit-bel-matati> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jnovotny>;
