<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/118758%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Iciniacum";
    rdfs:comment "The Roman fort at Theilenhofen, called Iciniacum in antiquity, was a Roman military camp along the Upper Germanic-Raetian Limes. The site lies to the northwest of the village of Theilenhofen in the Weißenburg-Gunzenhausen district of Bavaria. The fort was probably built in the middle of the third century CE.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/118758> .

