<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/122572946%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Walls of Caerwent (Venta Silurum)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79733%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The city walls of Venta Silurum (modern Caerwent) are among the best-preserved Roman period city walls in Britain. The walls were constructed around the 3rd century CE, augmenting an earlier earthwork defense system, with external towers added in the mid 4th century. ";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/122572946> .

