<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/122702818%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Mausoleum of Galla Placidia";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/393480%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "An ancient funerary chapel, part of the Santa Croce complex in Ravenna, Italy, possibly built as an imperial mausoleum (ca. AD 417 - 425). The empress Galla Placidia (d. AD 450 ) is the presumed, likely patron of the building, though she is very unlikely to have been entombed within one of three sarcophagi found inside.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/122702818> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/122702818/mausoleo-di-galla-placidia> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
