<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/122702818/sepulta-gallae-placidiae> dcterms:contributor <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/nkaye>;
    dcterms:description "Agnellus of Ravena, writing in the ninth century AD, was the first to name the funerary chapel in the San Croce complex in Ravenna, Italy, as the tomb of the empress Galla Placidia. His identification of the chapel as the burial place of the empress is widely contested.";
    dcterms:modified "2016-07-07T12:10:38-04:00";
    dcterms:title "Sepulcrum Gallae Placidiae";
    owl:sameAs <http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/122702818/sepulta-gallae-placidiae> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/122728089%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Buddhas of Bamyan";
    rdfs:comment "Monumental statues of Gautam Buddha were carved into the cliff-face at Bamyan, located in the Bamyan valley in the Hazarajat region of central Afghanistan, The statues were, respectively, 35 and 53 m tall. They were intentionally destroyed by the Taliban in 2001.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/122728089> .

