<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/130506468%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Step Gate of the Armory";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/360499819%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874621%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/882947620%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/945930916%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Nineveh's western wall had seven (or eight) gates: the Armory Gate (later Step Gate of the Armory) was the fifth gate from the northern city wall. The Neo-Assyrian king Sennacherib constructed it and gave it the Akkadian ceremonial names Pāqidat-kalāma (\"The One Who Regulates Everything\") and Lū-dāri-bānûša (\"May Its Builder Live Forever\").";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/130506468> .

