<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/132886213%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Palatine Stadium";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/971691208%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "\"Palatine Stadium\" is likely a misnomer when considering the probable function of this architectural complex located on the southeast corner of the Palatine Hill on the flank of the Domus Augustana-Flavia. Originating during the reign of the Domitian, this complex was restored numerous times, including during the reigns of Hadrian and Septimius Severus. As far as function goes, it may have been an elaborate, porticoed leisure garden.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/132886213> .

