<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/133324175%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Ešiddukišara";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893951%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/89975947%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The temple of the god Nabû, Ešiddukišara (“House of the Director of the Universe”), was located in the Tuba district of Babylon, in the western half of the inner city. According to the Babylonian topographical text Tintir = Babylon Tablet IV, it was one of three temples in that part of Babylon.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/133324175> .

