<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/136008628%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Pnyx fountain";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/205264674%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A rock-cut cistern on the southeast slope of the Pnyx hill in Athens, built in the late sixth century BC and supplied by the Peisistratid aqueduct. It received a mosaic floor in the second C AD. Dörpfeld identified it with the Enneakrounos fountain known from Classical literature, but this is disputed.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/136008628> .

