<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/138606%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Barzan (Gallo-Roman Site)";
    rdfs:comment "Site of a Gallo-Roman sanctuary and subsequent city of the Roman imperial period, the \"Site gallo-romain de Barzan\" is spread across the modern French communes of Barzan, Talmont-sur-Gironde and Arces-sur-Gironde in the department of Charente-Maritime. BAtlas equated it with ancient Tannum/Tamnum, but alternatives continue to be offered.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/138606> .

