<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/139029037%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Santa Maria in Monterone";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/635256113%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Santa Maria in Monterone is a Catholic church located in Rome's Sant'Eustachio neighborhood. The church gives its name to the street on which it is located. The church building is situated on first-century BCE ruins in the area of the artificial basin known as the stagnum Agrippae. The present edifice dates to 1682.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/139029037> .

