<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/14557445%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Köşk Höyük";
    rdfs:comment "Köşk Höyük is a limestone outcropping that was a site of human settlement that was terraced for that purpose in the neolithic period. The most recent layers date to the early Chalcolithic period (ca. 5000-4750 BCE), while earlier layers are Neolithic and date ca. 6300-5600 BCE.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/14557445> .

