    rdfs:label "Assur Archive 41";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893945%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "In the ruins of a private house outside the inner town wall in cC9I, excavators discovered a small archive consisting of 3 clay tablets and fragments as well as one clay envelope, dating to the mid-7th century BC. These texts are loan documents, as well as one list, which is a harvest report.";
