<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/155566866%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Paedagogium";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/364530240%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/792237246%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/971691208%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The so-called Pedagogium is a building that was part of the Flavian palace complex on the Palatine Hill. It was located below the exedra of the façade of the Domus Augustana. The Paedagogium is thought to have superseded the late-Republican domus known as the Domus Gelotiana.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/155566866> .

