<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/156485252%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Desert Gate";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874621%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/882947620%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/945930916%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Nineveh's western wall had seven (or eight) gates: the Desert Gate was the southernmost gate along that stretch of wall. The Neo-Assyrian king Sennacherib constructed it sometime between 695 and 691 B.C. and he gave it the Akkadian ceremonial name Kadrê-Tēme-u-Sumuʾel-qerebša-irrub (\"The Presents of the People of Tēma and Sumuʾel Enter Through It\").";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/156485252> .

