    rdfs:label "Brangues";
    rdfs:comment "A previously quarried limestone bed on the banks of the Rhone was identified and requarried in the 19th century near the modern French commune of Brangues in Isère. A number of discarded and incomplete stones were identified. The original quarrying has been assumed to have been of Roman date.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/167688> .

