    rdfs:label "Gilly-sur-Isère";
    rdfs:comment "An archaeologically attested \"agglomération romaine\" (evidently equipped with port and warehouse facilities) at modern Gilly on the Isere river in France (about 4km downriver from Albertville), appears to have been an extension or adjunct of the Roman road station and toll house of Ad Publicanos, thought to have been located in the area.";
