<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/175106248/ninurta-mukin-temmen-adussi-ana-labar-ume-ruquti> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jnovotny>;
    dcterms:description "Alternate name of the outer/lower city wall (šalḫû) of Dūr-Šarrukīn (\"Fort Sargon\") according to some Akkadian royal inscriptions of Sargon II (r. 721–705 BC). The Akkadian ceremonial name means \"The God Ninurta Is the One Who Establishes the Foundation of the Wall for (All) Days to Come.\"";
