<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/176836030%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Lefkandi Heroon(?)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/540909%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Rescue excavations in 1980 documented the remains of an unusual funerary structure dated ca. 1000 to 950 BCE that contained a double human burial alongside a horse burial. The structure's scale (50 by 13.8 m) and nature have led some scholars to identify it as a heroon.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/176836030> .

