<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/177113801%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Tumulus de Péré";
    rdfs:comment "The Péré tumulus, or Pairé tumulus, is a Neolithic tumulus that dates from the fifth millennium B.C. The site is located in Prissé-la-Charrière, in Deux-Sèvres, in New Aquitaine, France. It is composed of three main megalithic structures, built at different times.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/177113801> .

