<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/185031048%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Temple of Athena (Miletus)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/599799%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Temple of Athena in Miletos dates originally to the sixth century BCE, although the visible remains on site today belong to the Classical rebuilding of MIletos (ca. 479-450 BCE). The temple had a peripteral plan and was executed in the Ionic order. Unusually, its axis is oriented north-south.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/185031048> .

