<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/189727829%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Emeurur";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/5066376%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893951%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The temple of the goddess Nanāya, Emeurur (“House which Gathers the Me’s”), was located in the TE.E (read as either Tê or Kisīri) district of Babylon, in the eastern half of the inner city. According to the Babylonian topographical text Tintir = Babylon Tablet IV, it was the only temple in that part of Babylon.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/189727829> .

