<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/194496209%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Anavyssos";
    rdfs:comment "Anavyssos, Greece, is the findspot of the kouros of Kroisos, a fallen warrior. The kouros dates ca. 530–520 B.C. and is housed in the National Archaeological Museum of Athens (inv. no. 3851). The kouros was discovered in 1936.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/194496209> .

