    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/372769291%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "An ancient pyramid-shaped tomb built for Caius Cestius (ca. 18-12 BC), a magistrate and member of the Septemviri Epulonum. The tomb stands at the fork of the ancient Via Ostiensis and was later incorporated into the city's fortifications.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/195092807> .

