    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/808255902%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/905386158%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "In the present-day caldera, Nea Kameni is the larger of the two volcanogenic islands formed over the last two millennia. It is a geological successor of Cameini, and was likely formed before, or during, the major period of volcanic activity in 1866-1870.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/199559843> .

