    rdfs:comment "The House of Pansa (VI,6,1) is an atrium house in Pompeii that occupies an entire insula. Architectural elements date the structure ca. 140-120 BC in its original phase. The merchant and duumvir Cn. Alleius Nigidius Maius owned the property.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/19985870> .

