    dcterms:description "A Spanish village located to the west of Sevilla, Spain. In the thirteenth century, it belonged to the kingdom of Alfonso X. The modern toponym is a derivation of the Arabic toponym \"Solucar Al-bayda\", meaning \"the white one\". The site was known as Sanlúcar de Albaida until it took the definitive name of Albaida de Aljarafe.";
