    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/bender-h>;
    dcterms:description "The Roman fort at Theilenhofen, called Iciniacum in antiquity, was a Roman military camp along the Upper Germanic-Raetian Limes. The site lies to the northwest of the village of Theilenhofen in the Weißenburg-Gunzenhausen district of Bavaria. The fort was probably built in the middle of the third century CE.";
