    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "Sant Agustí Vell (also known as Poblat talaiòtic de Sant Agustí or \"Talayotic village of Sant Agustí\") is an archaeological site attributed to the Talayotic culture located in the municipality of Es Migjorn Gran in the south of the Balearic island of Menorca. It flourished between 850 BCE and the Roman invasion in 123 BCE.";
