    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/zrosalinsky>;
    dcterms:description "The Temple of Athena in Miletos dates originally to the sixth century BCE, although the visible remains on site today belong to the Classical rebuilding of MIletos (ca. 479-450 BCE). The temple had a peripteral plan and was executed in the Ionic order. Unusually, its axis is oriented north-south.";
